    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI think existing+planned navigation/jumping features in 'mini.nvim' together with built-in ways (like regular `w`, `b`, etc.) should be enough to cover this use case. In particular, 'mini.jump' and 'mini.jump2d' come to mind.\n\nFor sub-word *textobjects* (i.e. to act on the part of the word, not navigate), there are #1124 and #1434 that leverage 'mini.ai'. They are not quite easy to follow, but appear to do the job (only for Latin characters, though).\n\nSo I think I am going to close as not planned.",
